@moduledoc """
Burrito entry point — a thin shim over `ExRatatui.Burrito.main/3`, so
entry-point protocol fixes ship with ex_ratatui upgrades instead of
freezing here.

Runs as a supervised `Task` keyed on this module, so regenerating the
wiring stays idempotent and unrelated `Task` children are left alone.
The delegate is a no-op outside a burrito-wrapped binary (`mix test` and
`iex -S mix` never boot the TUI over the session), recognises
`--version` anywhere in argv for non-interactive smoke tests, and stops
the VM with a non-zero exit code when the TUI crashes or fails to start.
"""

use Task

@version Mix.Project.config()[:version]

def start_link(_arg) do
  Task.start_link(__MODULE__, :main, [Burrito.Util.Args.argv()])
end

def main(argv) do
  ExRatatui.Burrito.main(<%= inspect(@tui_module) %>, argv, name: "<%= @app %>", version: @version)
end
